        <p class="bj2-why-note">Every rebrand has a root cause. If one of these sounds like your business, this process was built to fix it.</p>
        <div class="bj2-why-grid">
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🏢</span><span class="bj2-why-num">01</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Forced by <strong>corporate change</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-external">External Trigger</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">New leadership, ownership transfer, or company pivot forces a brand reset to reflect the new direction and remove legacy associations.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🔀</span><span class="bj2-why-num">02</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Reflect <strong>structural realignment</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-strategic">Strategic</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">Spin-offs, department splits, or portfolio restructuring require each entity to have a distinct, standalone brand identity.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">⚔️</span><span class="bj2-why-num">03</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Forced by <strong>competition</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-external">External Trigger</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">A competitor rebranded or entered the space: staying put means being confused with them or losing perceived differentiation in the market.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🔭</span><span class="bj2-why-num">04</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Built from <strong>market insight &amp; gaps</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-strategic">Strategic</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">Research revealed an underserved niche or positioning gap. The rebrand repositions the business to own that space before a competitor does.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">👁️</span><span class="bj2-why-num">05</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Force <strong>change of perception</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-brand">Brand Equity</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">The current brand is associated with low quality, old pricing, or a wrong audience. A rebrand signals the business has fundamentally changed.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">📉</span><span class="bj2-why-num">06</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Forced by <strong>performance</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-internal">Performance</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">Sales are declining, leads are poor quality, or conversion is low. The brand is failing to attract or close the right clients and needs a strategic reset.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🔄</span><span class="bj2-why-num">07</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Driven by <strong>product life cycle</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-strategic">Strategic</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">The company expanded into new products or services that the current brand doesn't cover: a refresh or brand architecture update is needed to contain it all.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">✨</span><span class="bj2-why-num">08</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Seem more <strong>relevant &amp; authentic</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-brand">Brand Equity</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">The brand feels dated or inauthentic to today's audience. Founders want the visual and verbal identity to match who they've actually become.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🎯</span><span class="bj2-why-num">09</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">The need to <strong>simplify</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-brand">Brand Equity</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">Messaging is confusing, the logo is cluttered, or the offer is hard to explain. A rebrand strips it back to one clear, ownable idea that sells itself.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">©️</span><span class="bj2-why-num">10</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Clearer <strong>intellectual property</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-strategic">Strategic</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">The business needs to trademark, license, or franchise: the brand must be distinctive enough legally and visually to protect and scale.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">📊</span><span class="bj2-why-num">11</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Align with <strong>corporate strategy</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-strategic">Strategic</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">New 3 to 5 year goals, investor commitments, or market expansion plans require the brand to communicate ambition and credibility at a higher level.</div></div></div>
          <div class="bj2-why-card"><span class="bj2-why-icon">🤝</span><span class="bj2-why-num">12</span><div class="bj2-why-content"><div class="bj2-why-header"><div class="bj2-why-text">Reflect <strong>mergers &amp; de-mergers</strong></div><span class="bj2-why-badge bj2-badge-external">External Trigger</span></div><div class="bj2-why-desc">Two companies combining, or one splitting off, creates identity conflict. A unified or separated brand removes confusion and builds trust with both audiences.</div></div></div>
