  <div class="bm-faq-wrap" id="bm-faq" style="scroll-margin-top:68px">
<div class="bm-faq-head-row">
      <div class="bm-faq-icon-hero"><svg width="58" height="58" viewBox="0 0 58 58" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="58" height="58" fill="url(#faqiGrad)"/><path d="M22.5 23.2a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 12.9 1c0 4.2-4.6 4.7-4.6 8.4v1.1" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><rect x="28.9" y="39.4" width="3.4" height="3.4" rx="0.4" fill="#fff"/><defs><linearGradient id="faqiGrad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="58" y2="58" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop stop-color="#2536F5"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#7C3AED"/></linearGradient></defs></svg></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-head-txt">
        <div class="bm-eyebrow">FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="bm-section-title">Questions before every project</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="bm-section-sub">The things founders always ask before they start. Answered directly, no fluff.</p>
    <div class="bm-faq-cols">
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🛡️</span><span>How does the money-back guarantee actually work?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">If we miss the agreed delivery deadline, or the final delivery is materially incomplete versus the agreed scope, you get a full refund. No negotiation, no credit note. The only exceptions are delays caused by the client: late questionnaire submission or scope changes after commencement.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">💡</span><span>Why is there a RM290 entry offer? Is the quality lower?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">No. The entry offer exists to remove the risk of the first transaction. The RM290 logo mark uses the same methodology and team as a RM30,000 architecture project. The difference is scope, not quality. Most clients who start at RM290 move to a larger engagement within 60 days.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">⏱️</span><span>How long does a typical project take?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Entry offers deliver in 7 days. Websites deliver in 1 to 3 weeks depending on tier, and a scoped app build ships in about 3 weeks, our AI-accelerated workflow means projects now move in weeks, not months. Larger custom builds and full brand architecture have timelines agreed at kickoff. The clock starts from questionnaire submission, not from payment.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🗺️</span><span>Do you work with clients outside Kuala Lumpur?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Yes. The majority of our process is fully remote by design. Kickoff, reviews, and delivery happen via WhatsApp, email, and video call. We have active clients across Peninsular Malaysia, East Malaysia, and Singapore. In-person sessions are available for Klang Valley clients on request.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card bm-faq-extra" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">💳</span><span>What payment methods do you accept?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">We accept bank transfer, ToyyibPay, and DuitNow QR. For projects above RM5,000 we offer a 50/30/20 split: 50% to start, 30% at the halfway milestone, 20% on final delivery. Full upfront is not required for larger projects.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card bm-faq-extra" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">⚙️</span><span>What is Methodas and do I need it?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Methodas is our systems and education platform for founders who want to build without hiring an agency full-time. It gives you access to the same frameworks we use for clients. If you want it done for you, BrandMethod is for you. If you want to learn and build yourself, Methodas is for you. Many clients use both.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card bm-faq-extra" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🔄</span><span>How many revisions do I get?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Every project includes a defined number of revision rounds in the scope. Entry offers include one round. Growth and premium tiers include two to three. Revisions are based on the original brief. Direction changes after commencement are treated as scope changes and priced separately.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card bm-faq-extra" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🏆</span><span>How is BrandMethod different from Fiverr?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Fiverr delivers an asset. BrandMethod delivers a system. You get a dedicated PM, a written guarantee, a defined timeline, a growth pathway, and a Malaysian team that understands the local market and SME landscape specifically. The strategy behind the asset is what separates them.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">📂</span><span>Who owns the final files and the rights once it&rsquo;s done?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">You do, fully. On final payment you own every deliverable outright, including the editable master and source files. No licensing, no subscriptions, and no being locked into us to keep using your own brand. Any designer or developer can pick the files up later.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🧭</span><span>What do you need from me to get started?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">A completed onboarding brief, and for larger projects a short kickoff or strategy session. The brief takes anywhere from a few minutes to about an hour depending on the package, and the more honest and complete it is, the sharper the result. After that the work is largely on us, with clear checkpoints for your feedback.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">🧾</span><span>Will there be any hidden or extra costs?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">No surprises. Every package is fixed-price and quoted before you pay. The only separate costs are genuine third-party pass-throughs: government trademark fees, your ad spend, hosting, and those are billed at cost with no markup, and flagged upfront.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">⬆️</span><span>Can I start with a smaller package and upgrade later?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">Yes, and we build it so you&rsquo;re never penalised for starting small. Lower tiers credit toward higher ones: audit fees come off the build that follows, and website upgrade credit carries part of what you&rsquo;ve already paid into the bigger version. Start where you are and scale when it makes sense.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bm-faq-card" onclick="bmFaqToggle(this)">
      <div class="bm-faq-head"><span class="faq-emoji">📊</span><span>Do I have to pay the full amount upfront?</span><div class="bm-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></div></div>
      <div class="bm-faq-body"><div class="bm-faq-body-inner"><div class="bm-faq-body-text">For entry offers, yes, they&rsquo;re a single payment, which keeps them fast and low-risk. Larger projects run on 50/30/20 milestone payments: to begin, at the midpoint, and on final delivery, so what you pay tracks the progress of the work.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    </div>
